      "q": "2. Answer the following questions in about 30 words.\ni) Define human geography.",
      "a": "wer:\nHuman geography is the branch of geography which studies the relationship between the physical/natural and human worlds, the spatial distribution of human phenomena and how they come about, as well as the social and economic differences between different parts of the world.\nii) Name some sub-fields of human geography.\nAnswer:\nSome sub-fields of human geography include social geography, urban geography, political geography, population geography, settlement geography, economic geography, historical geography, medical geography, and behavioural geography.\niii) How is human geography related to other social sciences?\nAnswer:\nHuman geography is inter-disciplinary and develops close interfaces with other social sciences such as sociology, psychology, anthropology, economics, political science, and demography to understand and explain human activities and elements on Earth's surface."
