      "q": "3. Answer the following questions in not more than 150 words.\ni) Explain naturalisation of humans.",
      "a": "wer:\nNaturalisation of humans refers to the process where, in the early stages of their interaction with the environment, human beings were greatly influenced by nature. With low levels of technological development and primitive social conditions, humans adapted to the dictates of nature. This type of interaction, often seen in primitive or tribal societies, is termed environmental determinism.\nHere, nature is seen as a powerful force, worshipped, revered, and conserved. Human actions are guided by nature, for example, dependence on edible plants, worship of trees or natural forces, and the use of primitive tools for hunting. As people gain knowledge and advance technologically, they begin to move away from complete dependence on nature, creating opportunities and modifying the environment according to their needs.\nii) Write a note on the scope of human geography.\nAnswer:\nThe scope of human geography is vast as it covers the study of the spatial distribution and interrelationships of human phenomena\u2014the presence, patterns, and relationships between humans and their environment. Human geography is not just about the location of human activities but also explores how people interact with the physical world, and the resulting social and economic differences.\nIt incorporates both physical and man-made elements, examining how humans utilize natural resources, create settlements, and shape landscapes. The discipline is continuous and adaptive, responding to technological, social, and economic changes, and remains important in addressing global issues like sustainability, urbanization, and cultural integration. With its multi-disciplinary nature, human geography connects with various fields of social science to provide a holistic understanding of human existence on earth.\nMastering Human Geography: Nature and Scope\nGrasping the\nnature and scope of human geography\nis crucial for Class 12 success. Focus on understanding how humans interact with their environment, utilizing\nNCERT Solutions 2026-27\nto strengthen conceptual clarity.\nThis chapter highlights\nkey concepts\nlike environmental determinism, possibilism, and the interdisciplinary links of geography. Reviewing important definitions and examples helps you excel in board exams and builds a solid foundation for higher studies.\nRegular practice of exercise questions and focusing on\nfield and sub-fields of human geography\nensures a comprehensive grip on the subject. Use exam-oriented strategies to revise efficiently and boost your performance in Geography assessments.\nCBSE Class 12 Geography (Fundamentals of Human Geography) Chapter-wise NCERT Solutions\nS.No\nChapter-wise NCERT Solutions for Geography (Fundamentals of Human Geography) Class 12\n1\nChapter 2 The World Population Distribution Density and Growth Solutions\n2\nChapter 3 Human Development Solutions\n3\nChapter 4 Primary Activities Solutions\n4\nChapter 5 Secondary Activities Solutions\n5\nChapter 6 Tertiary And Quaternary Activities Solutions\n6\nChapter 7 Transport And Communication Solutions\n7\nChapter 8 International Trade Solutions\nCBSE Class 12 Geography Study Materials\nS.No\nStudy Materials for Class 12 Geography\n1\nCBSE Class 12 Geography NCERT Solutions\n2\nCBSE Class 12 Geography NCERT Book\n3\nCBSE Class 12 Geography PYQP"
