      "q": "2. Write a short note on the following in about 30 words.\n(i) High-Tech industry",
      "a": "wer:\nHigh-tech industries are those that apply intensive research and development to produce advanced scientific and engineering products. They feature highly skilled (white collar) workers, use of robotics, computer-aided design, and are often found in planned business parks known as technopolies.\n(ii) Manufacturing\nAnswer:\nManufacturing is the process of transforming raw materials into finished goods that have higher value. It encompasses a range from handicrafts to assembly-line mass production in factories, involving machinery, labour, and power to produce standardized products.\n(iii) Footloose industries\nAnswer:\nFootloose industries are those that can be located anywhere, as they are not dependent on specific raw materials. They rely on easy transportation of components, produce in small quantities, employ fewer workers, and are usually non-polluting. Accessibility by road is a key factor."
