      "q": "3. Answer the following questions in not more than 150 words.\ni. Discuss the significance and growth of the service sector in modern economic development.",
      "a": "wer:\nThe service sector, also called the tertiary sector, has become increasingly significant in modern economic development. In the early stages, most workers were engaged in the primary sector. As economies develop, more people shift to tertiary activities due to rising demand for professional services, trade, health, education, and communication.\nIn developed countries, a majority is employed in services, contributing substantially to GDP and economic growth. Services foster international trade, yield high monetary value through wages and charges, and provide significant foreign exchange. Infrastructure and specialized services such as retail, banking, IT, tourism, and consultancy play a crucial role. The expansion of the knowledge sector (quaternary and quinary activities) has created new job opportunities, shaped global economic patterns, and improved standards of living. Thus, the service sector is vital for both individual prosperity and national development.\nii. Explain in detail the significance of transport and communication services.\nAnswer:\nTransport and communication are pillars of the tertiary sector, essential for economic growth. Transport enables the movement of people, materials, and goods, enhancing accessibility and value at every production stage. Networks comprising nodes and links connect towns, cities, and markets, thereby aiding distribution and consumption. Transport increases the economic viability of industries and trade.\nCommunication services, involving the transmission of messages, facts, and ideas, are vital for coordination, connectivity, and information exchange. Advances in telecommunications like the internet, radio, and satellites have revolutionized communication, reducing time and cost, and enabling instant global connectivity. Mass media support advertising, education, and entertainment.\nEfficient transport and communication systems promote integration of regions, bring efficiency to administration, foster industrial and commercial growth, and support societal progress by reducing distances and bridging gaps.\nMastering Tertiary and Quaternary Activities in NCERT Geography\nThis chapter highlights the\nrole of services\nlike trade, transport, and ICT in shaping economies. By studying NCERT solutions, you can better understand\neconomic structure\nand prepare confidently for your Class 12 Geography exams.\nKey areas include\nmedical tourism\n, outsourcing, and the digital divide, often asked in board exams. Focus especially on differences between\nquaternary and quinary activities\nand their impact on global employment trends.\nPractice exercise-based\nNCERT solutions for Tertiary and Quaternary Activities\nregularly. This will help you improve your answer writing skills and boost your chances of scoring top marks in CBSE Class 12 Geography.\nCBSE Class 12 Geography (Fundamentals of Human Geography) Chapter-wise NCERT Solutions\nS.No\nChapter-wise NCERT Solutions for Geography (Fundamentals of Human Geography) Class 12\n1\nChapter 1 Human Geography Nature and Scope Solutions\n2\nChapter 2 The World Population Distribution Density and Growth Solutions\n3\nChapter 3 Human Development Solutions\n4\nChapter 4 Primary Activities Solutions\n5\nChapter 5 Secondary Activities Solutions\n6\nChapter 7 Transport And Communication Solutions\n7\nChapter 8 International Trade Solutions\nCBSE Class 12 Geography Study Materials\nS.No\nStudy Materials for Class 12 Geography\n1\nCBSE Class 12 Geography NCERT Solutions\n2\nCBSE Class 12 Geography NCERT Book\n3\nCBSE Class 12 Geography PYQP"
